# BDC Intelligence — environment variables
#
# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit .env.local.
# Leave these commented until a real value exists. Do not paste a database URI or a contact email here.

# Production web reader. A Supabase session or direct Postgres URI.
# The hosted client does not read this yet. The web process must not receive the pipeline URI.
# DATABASE_URL=

# Operator connection for migrations and pipeline writes. A Supabase session or direct Postgres URI.
# The hosted client does not read this yet. Keep it out of the web environment.
# PIPELINE_DATABASE_URL=

# Supabase Auth for the web sign-in (ADR 0015). Server-only: never add a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# Project URL and publishable key only. Do not add a service-role or secret key.
# Unrelated to DATABASE_URL; sign-in stays unavailable until both are set.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Canonical application origin for Microsoft OAuth redirectTo (no trailing path).
# Example: http://localhost:3000 locally, or the production BDC Flow origin.
# Required for Microsoft sign-in. Do not put Azure client secrets here.
# SITE_URL=

# Project name and contact email for SEC EDGAR fetches.
# Read by npm run sec:fetch and npm run registry:fetch. Those commands refuse to run without it.
# The value is not logged and is not written to the repository.
# SEC_USER_AGENT=
